;; Worklist item L1. The wave-2 gate (P-organise-the-library.md:636-638) noticed
;; that `:refused` was doing two jobs: refusing the EDGE (the directive line
;; leaves the pattern file) and refusing the WARRANT (the evidence is thin; the
;; edge stays proposed). The schema now separates them -- :state :refused for the
;; first, :state :proposed + :warrant-refused for the second
;; (library/.spider/attestation-schema.edn).
;;
;; This file classifies the five records that already carried :state :refused,
;; written before the distinction existed. Read by hand on 2026-09-01, no
;; verdict re-authored: the ACT each reviewer performed is read off what they did
;; to the pattern file, and the GROUND is quoted from their own :reason.
{:schema :library-contract/refusal-reclassification-v1
 :at "2026-09-01"
 :by "claude (library-build-loop work seat)"
 :item :L1
 :method
 "For each record: (1) locate its :state :refused row by file:line; (2) grep the
  source pattern's .flexiarg for a directive naming the target; (3) read the
  reviewer's own :reason for the ground they gave. Absent directive = the edge
  left the file = an edge-refusal was carried out."
 :finding
 "All five are true edge-refusals by act: no directive naming the target survives
  in any of the five source patterns. Two of them (aif rows 28 and 30) give a
  ground that is about the WARRANT, not the relation -- 'rung 1 by exact
  occurrence, but not a warrant'. Under the new vocabulary a reviewer with that
  ground could have chosen either act. Both reviewers chose to remove the
  directive, and that choice stands; it is recorded here, not revised, because
  the act was theirs and this pass is not a re-review."
 :records
 [{:record "library/aif/attestations.edn:479"
   :edge {:from "aif/structure-learning-by-model-reduction"
          :to "aif/posterior-variance-as-epistemic-value" :kind :how}
   :directive-in-file "not found (library/aif/structure-learning-by-model-reduction.flexiarg)"
   :act :edge-refusal
   :ground :relation-does-not-hold
   :ground-quote "the cited text ... does not mention the target; the edge reverses #14"}
  {:record "library/aif/attestations.edn:607"
   :edge {:from "aif/belief-state-operational-hypotheses"
          :to "writing-coherence/plain-language-thesis" :kind :see-also}
   :directive-in-file "not found (library/aif/belief-state-operational-hypotheses.flexiarg)"
   :act :edge-refusal
   :ground :warrant-insufficient
   :ground-quote "rung 1 by exact occurrence, but not a warrant"
   :note "Ground is warrant-shaped; the act carried out was edge-refusal. Under the
          new vocabulary this is the case a reviewer must now choose between."}
  {:record "library/aif/attestations.edn:646"
   :edge {:from "aif/expected-free-energy-scorecard"
          :to "ants/baseline-cyber-ant" :kind :see-also}
   :directive-in-file "not found (library/aif/expected-free-energy-scorecard.flexiarg)"
   :act :edge-refusal
   :ground :warrant-insufficient
   :ground-quote "rung 1 by exact occurrence, but not a warrant"
   :note "Same shape as the row at :607."}
  {:record "library/aif/attestations.edn:809"
   :edge {:from "aif/expected-free-energy-scorecard"
          :to "structure/mana-allostasis" :kind :see-also}
   :directive-in-file "not found (library/aif/expected-free-energy-scorecard.flexiarg)"
   :act :edge-refusal
   :ground :relation-does-not-hold
   :ground-quote "the patterns' IF/HOWEVER/THEN clauses do not supply a peer relation either"}
  {:record "library/writing-coherence/attestations.edn:95"
   :edge {:from "writing-coherence/meta-lede" :to "peeragogy/pattern-language" :kind :see-also}
   :directive-in-file "not found (library/writing-coherence/meta-lede.flexiarg)"
   :act :edge-refusal
   :ground :relation-does-not-hold
   :ground-quote "never relates it to pattern-language; the two conclusions share nothing"
   :repair "This record's :reason contained unescaped double quotes around
            \"meta-lede\", which split the EDN string and left `meta-lede` as a
            symbol key on the attestation map. Escaped on 2026-09-01; the linter
            now rejects a non-keyword attestation key so the class cannot recur
            silently."}]
 :not-touched
 [{:record "library/sidecar/attestations.edn:16 and :53"
   :why "The two sidecar holds carry an ad-hoc :refused-reason key with
         :state :proposed -- the warrant-refusal act written before it had a
         name. They are queued for a second read as worklist item L3, whose
         acceptance says to use this vocabulary; converting them here would
         pre-empt the reader's verdict."}]}
